  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The nature of the grant will be core funding to support WATHI&apos;s organisational mandate. The funding will also include a specific component on supporting prioritization of education reforms in West Africa with specific focus on the crucial role of teacher&#x2019;s training institutions, the challenges faced by public universities in the region and the aspirations of the youths in West Africa.In line with the approach of WATHI which calls both for an in-depth understanding of local contexts and expectations and the need to learn from experiences from countries around the world, WATHI proposes to stimulate the West African public debate on education and training.</narrative>
  </description>
